'''tormentor''' (tôr-men′tọr), ''n.'' [< ME. ''tormentour'', ''turmentour'', < OF. *''tormentour'' = Sp. ''tormentador'', < ML. *''tormentator'' (cf. ''tormentarius''), a torturer, < ''tormentare'', torment: see ''torment'', ''v.''] 1. One who or that which torments. {{smaller|Especially—(''a'') One whose office it is to inflict torture; an executioner.}}

{{smaller block|Then the lorde wonder loude laled & cryed,
& talkez to his ''tormenttourez:'' "takez hym," he biddez,
